# Rocketship styles

Reasons: `_planning/component-review-decisions.md`.

## Naming

- Block `rs-alert`, element `rs-alert__title`, modifier `rs-alert--error`.
- Every custom property starts with `--rs-`: token `--rs-space-4`, component variable `--rs-alert-bg`.

## Selectors

- Every compiled selector is one BEM class, plus pseudo-classes or pseudo-elements on that class: `.rs-table__body-row:nth-child(even)`, `.rs-checkbox::before`.
- Never: descendant `.rs-a .rs-b`, child `.rs-a > *`, sibling `.rs-a ~ .rs-b`, compound `.rs-a--x.rs-a__y`, tag `td`, ID `#x`.
- Nest with `&__element`, `&--modifier`, `&:state`.
- Never put an element inside a pseudo-class: `&:disabled { &__legend {} }` is wrong.
- No class in markup without a rule. The default variant has no modifier class.

## Change other parts through variables

- A modifier or state only reassigns `--rs-*` variables on the block. Elements read them:
  ```scss
  &--error { --rs-alert-bg: #{rs-token(color-danger-bg)}; }
  ```
- A row styles its cells the same way: `rs-table__foot-row` sets `--rs-table-cell-font-weight`; cells read it.
- A layout modifier moves elements through a variable: `grid-column: var(--rs-field-text-column, auto)`.
- A child reacting to parent state: the parent sets `--rs-<block>-<state>`; the child uses `@container style(--rs-<block>-<state>: value)`. Exact values only, never `>` or `<`.

## Tokens

- Write tokens only as `#{rs-token(name)}`, always inside `#{}`: `#{rs-token(space-4)}`.
- Never write a hex, px or rem value where a token exists. Never write your own `var()` fallback chain.
- Unknown token name: the build fails. Stop and ask Shane. Never invent a token.
- No token for the role you need: stop and ask Shane.
- Use a token only for the role in its name:
  - `color-*-fg`: text on the matching `color-*-bg`.
  - `color-*-accent`: strokes and fills. Never text.
  - `color-*-text`: text on page surfaces (`color-danger-text` for errors).
  - `color-border`: decorative lines. Control edges use `color-border-control`.
- Variant names describe the message, token names the palette role: Alert's `--error` reads `danger` tokens. Do not rename either.
- Never write `prefers-color-scheme` in a component.

## Component variables

Use only these two patterns:

- **Opt-in hook** (spacing, radius, border, type). Never assign it; read it with the token as fallback:
  `border-radius: var(--rs-alert-border-radius, #{rs-token(radius-md)});`
- **Variant-owned local** (colours modifiers swap). Assign on the block, reassign in modifiers:
  `--rs-alert-bg: #{rs-token(color-surface-elevated)};` then `background: var(--rs-alert-bg);`
  Consumers override a local on the block or one instance, never on bare `:root`.

## The style block

- Styles live in the component file. Astro: `<style is:global lang="scss">`. Svelte: `rocketship-svelte.mdc`. Never a separate `.scss` file.
- Import only the barrel: `@use '../styles/mixins' as *;`. Never a file inside `styles/mixins/`.
- Comments: `///` above the rule. Never `/* */` or `/** */`.
- Order in each rule: `--rs-*` variables, then `all: unset`, then `box-sizing`, then layout, then appearance.
- No inline `style="…"` or Svelte `style:` for design.

## Units

- Font sizes: `to-rem(18)`. Print styles may use `pt`.
- Everything else: `px`.
- Never `em` font sizes. To follow the context, `font-size: inherit`.

## Boundaries

- No outer margin.
- Never set `font-family`.
- Inline components (Label) set no `display`. A text container is never a flex row.
- Logical properties: `inline-size`, `padding-block-end`, `text-align: start`.
- Density: padding hooks only (`--rs-table-cell-padding-block`). Text never shrinks.

## Elements and text

- Every element class sets `margin: 0`.
- An element on a component background sets its own `color`.
- Body text (`__description`, `__hint`, `__error`): only `color`, `font-weight` if needed, `margin: 0`.
- Titles: `font-size: inherit`, a weight, `line-height: #{rs-token(line-height-tight)}`, `color`, `margin: 0`.
- `th` and `caption` classes set `text-align: inherit` or `start`.

## States

- Nest states under the block or modifier: `&:hover`, `&:focus-visible`, `&:disabled`.
- Focus: `&:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #{rs-token(color-focus-ring)}; outline-offset: 2px; }`.
- Static content has no hover state.
